at if you I don't think that's a  fair question and I think that if you  talk to experts dr. Falchi dr. Burks and  others the models and in many cases are  way off in the new york city we actually  have people on the ground who have told  us that there are a thousand ventilators  sitting in a warehouse right now and  haven't been used you heard Governor  Cuomo yesterday say look we actually  have resources they're just mismatched  and so we sent a team a FEMA team to  help New York City make sure the  resources are getting to where they need  I talk to people in western New York who  said they're furlough and nurses and  hospitals in western New York State and  while people in New York City are  suffering we need to make sure we get  the right resources to the right people  and that's what we're committed to do oh  yeah please with the government's  response dr. Adams based on what you're  saying to us right now you pleased with  how things are going well pleased is I  don't think a fair word because gosh  there are people dying my colleagues out  there suffering I'm not pleased with the  with with the entirety of the response  because it takes state and federal and  people come together I take out pleased  are you satisfied pardon are you  satisfied with how things are going I'm  not gonna be satisfied until we get till  the to the end of this and we see  cooperation at every level and we see  health care workers getting what they  need dr. Adams you mentioned hotspots  and at the same time the administration  is putting out a letter to Governor  saying they may have tears for risk  different areas of the country would  open others would not given the lack of  testing in many areas and given that one  patient moving from one hotspot to a non  hotspot can ignite a whole new outbreak  how realistic is it really to have those  tears how you gonna do that I'm gonna be  bans on movement well you heard dr.  Burks say yesterday that 19 out of our  50 states about 40 percent of the  population of our country has been doing  surveillance testing and has shown  consistently low rates of spread of  coronavirus we also know that the local  authorities are the ones who make those  decisions I used to run a state the  Health Department for a State Health  Department for three years we want to  get people the tools they need to make  the right decisions and right now there  are some places that are going to be New  York City there are other places that  are going to see low spread and we want  them to have the the information to make  the right decisions and we're not going  to make those decisions from DC we're  going to give them the tools the advice  the data and it's going to be up to them  to decide what they do thank you very  much dr. Adams for being with us
 

